    "weaker": [],
    "explanation": "Tyrande is great on smaller maps like Dragon Shire or Tomb of the Spider Queen that focus a lot on early game rotations. These frequent skirmishes also help her stack Lunar Flare's Quest early. Thanks to Hunter's Mark and Lunar Flare, she excels at taking down enemy Heroes with other crowd control abilities.\n\nHunter's Mark can also be applied to non-Heroic targets, such as Bosses, Immortals, or Punishers, which makes Tyrande a powerful pick on Battlefield of Eternity. When combined with Trueshot Aura, your team can quickly burn these high-Health targets during the 40% extra damage window. She is also excellent on maps where Objectives keep Minions nearby, allowing safer cooldown refunds while healing her team, such as Infernal Shrines or Tomb of the Spider Queen."
  },
  "builds": [
    {
      "name": "Hunter Build",
      "label": "Recommended",
      "description": "Tyrande's Hunter Build focuses on maximizing Hunter's Mark uptime to enable multiple Lunar Flare casts during team fights. It also provides strong healing through the Level 4 and Level 7 Talents, especially when you can attack without being punished.\n\nThis build encourages frequent use of Lunar Flare during team fights, enabled by the cooldown reduction from Ranger's Mark. In most fights, place Hunter's Mark on the enemy Tank to heal your frontline while applying pressure. When your frontline engages, use Hunter's Mark and immediately activate Trueshot Aura. Save the refreshed Hunter's Mark to follow up on another target if the original Mark target can no longer be hit.",
